%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a0b39fb047c6fa040bb2f031da1e5ed1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Quest_TitheBarnShortfall
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Game::Game.Quest.QuestSO
  questId: TitheBarnShortfall
  title: Counted Twice
  description: Reeve Pell counts the tithe barn at dusk and again at dawn, and every week the dawn count comes up short. The lock is never forced. Pell wants the thief's name, and until he has it, everyone new is on his list.
  startPart:
    fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8c9ac901c412a54b961d69fc50dfbe6, type: 2}
    entry: Reeve Pell's tithe barn is short every dawn, and the lock is never forced. He'll pay for the thief's name.
  completedParts:
  - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e4b30bd6eee0339409afaecd06ae723a, type: 2}
    entry: 'I gave Pell the thief''s name: Osric Venn, a garrison guard with a key to the barn.'
  - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cae7dd430b7513a4cb9f63344d8049ff, type: 2}
    entry: I gave Pell a name, just not the right one. Pim from the field gang will pay for Venn's sacks.
  failedParts:
  - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4cef2c1fbf261d044a5735d90fc634a8, type: 2}
    entry: Venn is dead. Whatever he knew about the barn went into the ground with him.
  steps:
  - title: Ask around the farm
    description: Pell wants me to ask the field gang, who work next to the barn every day, and Venn, the guard on the fields gate.
    parts:
    - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f38602beba8a6945bd7869fc97d4ee5, type: 2}
      entry: Pim says nobody watches the barn once the gang is out. Anyone hungry enough could slip in.
    - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 365756376a0886041a7d2a3a3bda70b4, type: 2}
      entry: Gerrit doesn't think it's a worker, since they'd be the first suspected. It's someone who knows the place well, though. Someone nobody counts.
    - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 34e97a5740a4dab4ca7a7995a34e071c, type: 2}
      entry: Venn at the fields gate blames the poor workers on the strips. He's seen nothing, he says, and he'd rather I stopped asking.
  - title: A man with a key
    description: Aldric the cook hears what sells in the camp after dark. He might know where Pell's grain goes.
    parts:
    - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a6f60fe3c7e29b24b86e9d053a369f8e, type: 2}
      entry: Aldric says the barn grain reaches the gang's tent after midnight, carried by a man who didn't need to climb in.
  - title: Watch the barn
    description: Whoever empties the barn does it at night. Wait by the tithe barn after midnight.
    parts:
    - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4d1bd5f652da10e449b0a1e4ebcaeb8a, type: 2}
      entry: I caught Osric Venn, a garrison guard, carrying sacks out of the tithe barn with his own key.
  - title: Pell wants proof
    description: Pell won't take a newcomer's word against a Company guard.
    parts:
    - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 553a94b1dd55371429a3560d8470a992, type: 2}
      entry: Pell won't believe me without proof. If Venn takes the grain, someone buys it. I need something with his name on it.
  - title: Something with his name on it
    description: Whoever takes Pell's grain sells it, and whoever buys it may keep a record.
    parts:
    - fact: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0f6517e2926a3a74584df5eca8ccb8ab, type: 2}
      entry: 'I took Brann''s grain tally from his stash. Every week the same line: O.V., three sacks, twelve coin.'
